From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 00:13:41 -0400
Subject: feat: site icons in the command bar's rows (GitHub issue 58)

Each row in tabs mode starts with an icon: an open tab's own, the
page's icon from the profile's favicons for a closed tab, a History or
Bookmark suggestion, a typed site and a blank document, the magnifier
for a search and the information glyph for site information. A lookup
is made once per page per bar and its answer replaces the default page
icon in place, without rebuilding the list. A browser page's glyph is
drawn in the bar's secondary text colour. Actions mode draws no icons.
What a row says besides its title -- "Switch to Tab", the Space, the
kind of suggestion, a chord -- is now its own smaller label at the
row's right end, and the Independent-session mark follows the Space's
name there.

Why: GitHub issue 58; the owner said yes on 2026-10-30 (BACKLOG S-361):
the rows could only be told apart by reading them.
Removable when: never as a feature; the rows are Stedding's own views.
